# Force Mutter to pick the NVIDIA dGPU as the primary (compositing) GPU.
#
# Mutter 46 chooses a "primary" GPU at session start. Its default heuristic
# (MetaBackendNative / meta_backend_native_get_primary_gpu) prefers the GPU
# that drives the builtin panel — on this AORUS-15-9MF that is the Intel iGPU
# (card1, eDP-1), producing this gnome-shell log line:
#
#     GPU /dev/dri/card1 selected primary from builtin panel presence
#
# Mutter also honors an explicit udev override: a DRM device tagged
# "mutter-device-preferred-primary" wins over the builtin-panel heuristic.
# When the override fires, the log line changes to:
#
#     GPU /dev/dri/card2 selected primary given udev rule
#
# (Tag name + both log strings verified in libmutter-14.so.0.0.0, mutter 46.2.)
#
# Match strategy: do NOT match on KERNEL=="card2" — the cardN index is not
# stable across boots. Match the NVIDIA DRM *card* node structurally:
#   - SUBSYSTEM=="drm"            : DRM subsystem
#   - KERNEL=="card[0-9]*"        : a card node (not renderD12x, not a connector)
#   - ENV{DEVTYPE}=="drm_minor"   : the drm minor, not card1-eDP-1 style children
#   - DRIVERS=="nvidia"           : bound to the proprietary nvidia driver
#   - ATTRS{vendor}=="0x10de"     : PCI vendor NVIDIA (belt-and-suspenders)
#
# This targets the RTX 4050 Mobile at PCI 0000:01:00.0 (ATTRS{device}==0x28a1)
# without hard-coding the card index or the device id.

ACTION=="add|change", SUBSYSTEM=="drm", KERNEL=="card[0-9]*", ENV{DEVTYPE}=="drm_minor", DRIVERS=="nvidia", ATTRS{vendor}=="0x10de", TAG+="mutter-device-preferred-primary"
